# The oldest compiler that can still compile this tree. A stage0 reports its
# version on RUST's line (that is what `-V` speaks), never on Trust's
# MAJOR.MINOR.0 line, so this floor and src/rust-compat-version are what it is
# measured against — not src/version. Raise it when the tree starts depending on
# a newer upstream feature.
#
# Trust: 1.100.0 since 2026-11-03 (DQ SEED-BRIDGE-1). The 1.99-line seed
# shims are gone, so no 1.99 toolchain compiles the tree: from the 0.11.0-trust
# seed (`release: 1.99.0-dev`, 20565c3255), with this floor put back at 1.99.0,
# `x.py check --stage 1` stops at E0658 on `!` (`never_type`) in rustc_serialize,
# the first crate whose shim this tree no longer carries (2026-11-04). Two
# stage0s measured on it: the 0.12.0-trust seed pinned below (`release:
# 1.101.0-dev`, 29ebb403de) and stock 1.100.0-beta.7 (fd8e211ae, the DDC oracle;
# the `-beta.7` suffix is dropped before the comparison, as `-dev` is; from it
# `x.py check --stage 1 compiler/rustc` passes, its tools were not checked).
# 1.101.0 would refuse that oracle, so the floor is the 1.100 line.
min_stage0_rustc_version=1.100.0

# The independently supported running Cargo/Targo planner floor, not the Rust
# compiler needed to compile either this tree or Cargo itself. The retained
# native D23032 planner reports 1.98.0 and has actually built the current
# Bootstrap/Targo source. Its planner API is independent of the 1.100 compiler
# never_type floor above. Older planners remain unsupported; this is a measured
# supported floor, not a claim that all older versions lack a particular flag.
# Actual command/capability probes and failures remain mandatory. Keep the
# existing rust-compat-version ceiling for unqualified future tool versions.
min_stage0_cargo_version=1.98.0

